{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1259433-shadow-mechanics-for-wr20","id":1259433,"title":"Shadow mechanics for Wr20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-10-07T10:30:02-07:00","id":1259433,"title":"Shadow mechanics for Wr20","content":"I'm planning on getting Wraith 20 this Christmas, but one thing I'm dying to know (no pun intended) is whether or not the mechanics have been updated/altered for how the shadow is handled in roleplaying. This is particularly relevant for me because I am trying to get my troupe to play Wraith and--assuming they are game for the setting which can at times be demoralizing--I know that the shadow-roleplaying can be off-putting or intrusive for many.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","name":"Trategos_Sol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T15:39:33-07:00","id":1259476,"title":"","content":"Can you get someone to help you by playing as Shadowguide for the all the other players? I've found it works well for newer folks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-10T03:05:57-07:00","id":1259940,"title":"","content":"The book offers a couple different options, including Deterministic Shadowguiding, where shadow interference is handled by the DM according to the shadows' angst ratings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T11:41:59-08:00","id":1266465,"title":"","content":"for most of my games, i allow the player to choice to either to start by rolling there permanent Will Power (Diff 6) to determine there starting Permanent Angst or start with 1 Permanent Angst and TA = to WP, this i have found gives the players enough rope to hang themselves with as they think &quot;oh I only have a little Angst and this Arcani only gives a little more&quot; so they dont manage there Angst as much and start down the road to Oblivion all the faster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24734-deadman","name":"DeadMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}